{{!< default}}
{{!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  post.hbs — THE DISPATCHER.

  Ghost gives a theme exactly one post.hbs for every post on the site. This
  site has several kinds of post that are genuinely different PAGES — a lesson
  is a reading player, a course is a sales page, a doc is a reference — so
  this file renders nothing itself. It reads tags and dispatches.

  ⚠️ BRANCH ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. #training-section is tested BEFORE
  #training-content, because a section overview is not a lesson and matching
  the lesson branch would render it inside the lesson player. A new branch
  goes where its SPECIFICITY demands, not at the end: ask whether any post
  carries both this tag and one already in the list, and if so put the more
  specific one first. Read abstract/02 before adding one.

  Only the fallback surface is built so far, so every branch that has no
  partial yet is commented rather than pointing at a file that does not exist
  — a missing partial is a 500, not a fallback. Uncomment a line in the same
  commit that adds its partial.

      {{#has tag="documentation"}}          {{> "post-documentation"}}
      {{else has tag="#training-section"}}  {{> "post-training-section"}}
      {{else has tag="#training-content"}}  {{> "post-training"}}
      {{else has tag="#course"}}            {{> "post-course"}}
      {{else has tag="#lesson"}}            {{> "post-lesson"}}
      {{else has tag="#resource"}}          {{> "post-resource"}}
      {{else has tag="#blog"}}              {{> "post-blog"}}

  Note that default.hbs forks on the SAME tags to swap the chrome, so a
  reading surface does not get a marketing bar. The two lists must stay in
  agreement — if a kind of post moves from marketing chrome to reading chrome,
  it changes in both files or the page gets a bar that contradicts its body.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#post}}
  {{> "post-default"}}
{{/post}}
